<title>USA: CBOT Jan volume falls 3.3 percent year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CBOT Jan volume falls 3.3 percent year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Board of Trade said volume in its futures and options totaled 18,991,093 contracts in January, down 3.3 percent from 19,648,715 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Volume in major categories and in selected individual contracts is as follows, with volume for January 1997 and percentage change followed by January 1996 volume:  </p>
<p>All futures     14,560,597     - 3.3     15,056,621</p>
<p>  Agricultural   3,594,540     -25.8	4,845,902</p>
<p>  Financial     10,962,299     + 7.4     10,203,415</p>
<p>All options on</p>
<p>	 futures   4,430,496     - 3.5	4,592,094</p>
<p>  Agricultural     936,213     -28.9	1,317,000</p>
<p>  Financial	3,493,706     + 6.7	3,274,255</p>
<p>Futures (individual)</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     8,104,708     + 7.7	7,528,607</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes 1,780,505     + 8.0	1,649,113</p>
<p>  US 5-yr notes    927,532     +10.8	  837,255</p>
<p>  Wheat		312,680     -50.2	  628,34</p>
<p>  Corn	     1,160,623     -41.7	1,992,182</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 1,119,782     -14.0	1,302,564</p>
<p>  Soymeal	    479,001     - 3.5	  496,414</p>
<p>  Soyoil	     473,290     +33.5	  354,602</p>
<p>Options</p>
<p>  US T-bonds     2,746,139     +23.7	2,219,841</p>
<p>  US 10-yr notes   542,336     -32.0	  797,383</p>
<p>  Corn		 373,634     -38.7	  609,803</p>
<p>  Soybeans	   385,208     -13.0	  442,750</p>
</text>
